inquiry: true
---
{% from "partials/enterprise/macros.njk" import arrow, ph %}
{% from "partials/enterprise/icons.njk" import icon %}
{%- set faqs = [
  ["Can network security testing identify risks before attackers exploit them?", "Yes. Network Security Testing Services help identify exposed systems and security weaknesses before attackers can take advantage of them. Early identification gives businesses time to address vulnerabilities and reduce the risk of unauthorized access or service disruption."],
  ["Can network security testing find weaknesses in our office network?", "Yes. Testing can identify weak access controls and insecure network configurations along with exposed devices and outdated systems within an office network. The assessment helps IT teams understand which areas need stronger protection."],
  ["How does network security testing help prevent data breaches?", "Network security testing identifies weaknesses that could allow unauthorized users to access business systems or sensitive information. By addressing these issues, organizations can reduce opportunities for attackers to enter the network and reach confidential data."],
  ["Can network security testing detect risks caused by incorrect firewall settings?", "Yes. A network security assessment can identify firewall rules that allow unnecessary connections or provide broader access than required. Correcting these settings helps restrict network traffic and reduce exposure to potential attacks."],
  ["Is network security testing useful for businesses that already have a firewall and antivirus software?", "Yes. Firewalls and antivirus software provide important protection, but they may not detect every network weakness. Network Security Testing Services help identify gaps in configurations and access controls that could remain even when security tools are in place."],
  ["Can network security testing assess risks from remote employees and VPN connections?", "Yes. Depending on the agreed scope, testing can examine remote access arrangements and VPN configurations to identify weak authentication or excessive permissions that could expose business systems to unauthorized access."],
  ["What happens if critical vulnerabilities are discovered during network security testing?", "Critical findings are documented and communicated according to the agreed reporting and escalation process. Your IT team can then prioritize corrective action based on the severity of the issue and its potential impact on business operations."],
  ["Does network security testing require business systems to go offline?", "Most assessments can be planned to minimize disruption to normal business activities. Testing methods and schedules are agreed upon in advance, and potentially disruptive activities require appropriate authorization and safeguards."],
  ["How often should network security testing be performed?", "Testing is recommended after major network changes and infrastructure upgrades along with significant security incidents. Periodic assessments also help identify weaknesses introduced by new devices and configuration changes as the network evolves."],
  ["What should a business prepare before starting network security testing?", "Businesses should define the testing scope and identify the network assets included in the assessment. Providing relevant network diagrams and authorized access details along with approved testing windows helps the assessment proceed efficiently."],
  ["Can network security testing help meet security compliance requirements?", "Network security testing can support security and compliance initiatives by identifying vulnerabilities and documenting corrective actions. The specific requirements depend on the applicable framework and the organization's regulatory obligations."]
] %}

