<section class="section section--paper" id="types" aria-labelledby="s2-title">
  <div class="container">
    <header class="shead">
      <div class="shead__meta"></div>
      <div class="shead__body">
        <h2 class="shead__title rv" id="s2-title">Types of Network Security Testing Services</h2>
        <p class="shead__lede rv" style="--d:1">CipherTrivia offers Network Security Testing Services to help businesses identify vulnerabilities across their IT infrastructure and reduce the risk of unauthorized access. Our assessments cover network devices and security configurations along with exposed services and access controls to help organizations protect critical systems and sensitive business data.</p>
      </div>
    </header>

    <div class="ledger ledger--7">
      <article class="ledger__cell rv">
        <div class="ledger__head">{{ icon("network") }}</div>
        <h3 class="ledger__title">Internal Network Security Testing</h3>
        <p class="ledger__text">We assess internal network environments to identify security gaps that could allow attackers or unauthorized users to access business systems. The testing focuses on device security and access permissions along with weaknesses that could enable threats to spread across the network.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="ledger__cell rv" style="--d:1">
        <div class="ledger__head">{{ icon("globe") }}</div>
        <h3 class="ledger__title">External Network Security Testing</h3>
        <p class="ledger__text">Our external network assessments identify security weaknesses visible from outside the organization's network. We examine internet-facing systems and exposed services to uncover potential entry points that attackers could target.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="ledger__cell rv" style="--d:2">
        <div class="ledger__head">{{ icon("target") }}</div>
        <h3 class="ledger__title">Network Penetration Testing</h3>
        <p class="ledger__text">Through authorized attack simulations, we evaluate how network vulnerabilities could be exploited to gain unauthorized access or compromise connected systems. The findings help businesses understand potential attack paths and prioritize security improvements.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="ledger__cell rv" style="--d:3">
        <div class="ledger__head">{{ icon("firewall") }}</div>
        <h3 class="ledger__title">Firewall Security Assessment</h3>
        <p class="ledger__text">We review firewall rules and network traffic controls to identify misconfigurations and unnecessary access permissions. This helps organizations reduce network exposure and restrict connections to approved services and systems.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="ledger__cell rv">
        <div class="ledger__head">{{ icon("wifi") }}</div>
        <h3 class="ledger__title">Wireless Network Security Testing</h3>
        <p class="ledger__text">Our wireless security testing evaluates Wi-Fi configurations and access controls to identify weaknesses that could expose business networks to unauthorized connections. The assessment helps improve wireless protection and reduce risks associated with insecure network access.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="ledger__cell rv" style="--d:1">
        <div class="ledger__head">{{ icon("radar") }}</div>
        <h3 class="ledger__title">Network Vulnerability Assessment</h3>
        <p class="ledger__text">Our Network Vulnerability Assessment identifies known security weaknesses across network infrastructure and connected systems. Findings are classified by severity to help organizations prioritize remediation based on risk and potential business impact.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="ledger__cell rv" style="--d:2">
        <div class="ledger__head">{{ icon("segments") }}</div>
        <h3 class="ledger__title">Network Segmentation Testing</h3>
        <p class="ledger__text">We evaluate how effectively internal networks separate critical systems and sensitive resources. The assessment identifies access control gaps that could allow unauthorized movement between network segments and increase the impact of a security incident.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

